Runs the test with serializable reads, so Jepsen catches stale reads.

A serializable read is answered by the node from its own copy, without the
leader. A node cut off from the majority by a partition answers with a value
the majority has already replaced, and the history is not linearizable.
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, like the example.

Apply it from this directory, before building the disk:

    git apply stale-reads.patch

and take it out again with:

    git apply -R stale-reads.patch

--- a/docker-compose.yml
+++ b/docker-compose.yml
@@ -40,6 +40,7 @@

   control:
     image: jepsen-control:local
+    command: ["sh", "start.sh", "--reads", "serializable"]
     depends_on:
       n1: {condition: service_healthy}
       n2: {condition: service_healthy}
